From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:02:43 +0000
Subject: Widgets: place a stereo window when its ancestors move, not inside the flush

A stereo QOpenGLWidget gets a native window of its own under alien ancestors
(stereo3d-native-stereo-opengl-widget.patch), and its ancestors do not move that
window when they move. That patch placed the window inside
QWidgetRepaintManager::flush() of the window. On Wayland the move exposed the
parent window synchronously; the nested repaint rebuilt the top level's texture
lists and freed the list that flush() then handed to rhiFlush(). Memcheck of
FreeCAD's stress run showed 31 error contexts reading a freed
QPlatformTextureList; the recipe's test tests/stereo-widget-move shows the same
31 in a scroll area, a graphics view's viewport and an item view.

The window is now placed when the geometry of an ancestor changes, the way Qt
keeps a window container in place (QWindowContainer's markParentChain() and
parentWasMoved(), called from QWidget::move() and QWidget::setGeometry()): the
widgets from a stereo window up to its window carry a bit of QWExtra,
hasStereoWindow, beside hasWindowContainer, and move(), setGeometry(),
setParent() and QWidget::scroll() of a marked widget place the stereo windows
below it. setWSGeometry(), which QWidget::scroll() uses, gives a stereo window
its place in its native parent, not in its alien parent. This patch changes
code added by stereo3d-native-stereo-opengl-widget.patch; it is a patch of its
own because a successor of a published source only appends to the series.

Measured against the other place, the move queued until the flush returned,
both with o863-0001 (upstream's subsurface move without a synchronous expose)
and without it, in the test's four shapes (row 863): every place leaves no
freed-list read; only this place with o863-0001 has every stereo window placed
after every step in every shape, and no commit of the parent that showed a
stereo window away from its widget in the scroll area and the item view (60
and 62 such commits per 60 steps with the published build, 42 against 60 in
the viewport shape). The queued move left a window at its old place for a
whole step in the scroll area and the item view.

Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-24
Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
